+# 20261112-001 — selection caller resize lifetime (code r136)
+
+## Purpose / reason
+
+Continue plan024 stage1 from r135 without overwriting prior WIP. Important policy, current plan, historical plan, renderer Source/PlusCal and relevant Mantine/public layout contracts were read fully in chunks. Public selection's delayed synthetic global resize bypassed the renderer's existing requesting-host/operation lifetime guard and could refresh a successor workspace.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Public setSelectedSlot schedules the existing scoped renderer resize immediately after final supplied workspace handoff. Rejection remains silent; selection/Project semantics unchanged.
+- Extend existing regression160 with actual public caller, final-state identity, stale/current resize and rejection checks. No new tests/suites.
+- Increment code135 to136 with canonical-LF fingerprint and review; keep stale and preserve upper lineage. Append plan024 progress; add focused review.
+- `.patch` is an incremental diff against bytes immediately before this unit (not HEAD), including new review and this explanation. It excludes itself and all pre-existing WIP/patches. The local snapshot used to derive it is removed after patch generation.
+
+## Alternatives rejected
+
+- Delaying the global event still permits broad observer refresh and wrong lifetime acquisition.
+- A new resize queue/token/projection cache duplicates renderer ownership already present.
+- Removing resize entirely omits the explicit Source/PlusCal selection obligation.
+- Source/PlusCal/policy changes are unnecessary: this is a lower-layer correspondence fix.
+
+## Checks / omissions
+
+Static diff/whitespace and independent canonical byte hashes only. Baseline r135 hash reproduced; r136 `sha256:88a9efa34356b8e38b355e8f8b18f1ae7a844f09a80aaac86202cc6f15ec5acc`. Authored fixture not executed. No local app/test/build/checker, Actions, commit/push, delegation, dist or policy changes. Code remains stale; stage1 remains open. Native browser/Plotly/mounted UI/inline-split integration and official lineage validation await separately authorized execution.
+
